{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles country-wise and level-wise counts of foreign students (based on actual response) enrolled in India, covering all levels as well as under graduate, post graduate, M.Phil., and Ph.D. by gender (male and female). It supports analysis of international student participation across academic levels and source countries. Published by the Ministry of Education, Department of Higher Education, the information is provided for India (national coverage).",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Higher Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers subscriber coverage under the Swavalamban Scheme, focusing on enrolment through aggregators appointed under the Pension Fund Regulatory and Development Authority (PFRDA). It captures the entities involved in enrolling unorganised-sector subscribers and facilitating contributions under the co-contributory pension framework. Published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Financial Services, the information supports monitoring of scheme reach and aggregator participation across India (national coverage).",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Pension Reforms"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on COVID-19 patient information for Indore, covering cases managed at input hospitals under the Smart Cities Mission. It supports public health monitoring and situational awareness by organizing records related to COVID patients and corona patients. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, with Madhya Pradesh and Indore in scope, the resources are city-specific and intended for use in tracking and understanding hospital-level COVID-19 burden.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Crime in India compiles annual, India-wide statistics on crime registration, investigation and case disposal across IPC and Local & Special Law categories. It covers major offences such as murder and culpable homicide, kidnapping and abduction, rape, and property-related crimes, along with related victim profiles and court/trial details. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB), the series supports trend analysis, policy planning, and monitoring of law-and-order outcomes from 1953 to 2023 (67 editions).",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Police"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog presents Institutional Households by Household Size from the Census 2001 for India and States. It focuses on counts of institutional households and their distribution across household-size categories, supporting demographic analysis and planning. The data are published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, Department of Home, through the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India. Coverage spans India (national coverage) with state-level breakdowns aligned to Census 2001.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Motor Transport Statistics compiles time-series information on road transport in India, covering registered motor vehicles, road accidents (persons killed and injured), and the physical and financial performance of State Road Transport Undertakings (SRTUs). It also tracks licensing indicators such as valid drivers’ and conductors’ licences, along with revenue realised from road transport and related infrastructure measures such as the length of national highways. Published by the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways, the series spans from 1970-71 to 2001-2002.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Covers non-workers classified by main activity, age and sex for the 1991, 2001 and 2011 Census. It presents gender-wise and age-group-wise counts of non-workers such as students, household duties, dependents, retired persons/pensioners, rentiers, beggars and vagrants. Produced by the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India under the Ministry of Home Affairs, the tables support demographic analysis of labour-force participation patterns and planning for social and welfare needs across India (national coverage).",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Tracks the number of newly registered motor vehicles and the total number of registered motor vehicles across 35 States/UTs. Vehicles are classified into Transport and Non Transport categories, supporting analysis of fleet growth and registration trends by category. Published by the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways, the indicators are useful for transport planning, policy monitoring, and understanding regional changes in vehicle ownership and registration. Geographic coverage spans all listed States/UTs.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers solid waste management for Chennai, Tamil Nadu, focusing on end-to-end operations from source segregation to door-to-door (D2D) collection. It addresses bin placement and sizes, collection vehicle types and capacities, and the processing and disposal options for collected waste. The scope supports planning and performance assessment of municipal sanitation services, including waste handling for households. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, it is city-specific for the City of Chennai.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Municipal Waste, Water and Sanitation; Sanitation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Union Budget datasets provide India’s annual fiscal statements and related budget estimates, including revenue and expenditure, receipts, taxes, deficits, and subsidy allocations. Published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs, these materials support analysis of fiscal policy, budgeting, and public finance trends. The catalog covers the Union Budget editions 2018-19, 2021-22, 2022-23, and 2023-24, with India (national coverage) as the geographic scope.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Revenue"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Union Budget: 2019-20 (Interim) compiles the annual financial statement presented for the Republic of India, covering key budget aggregates such as receipts, expenditure, and deficit. It supports understanding of government fiscal priorities and interim budget allocations for the 2019-20 period. Published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs, the budget information is intended for policymakers, researchers, and citizens tracking public finance and fiscal performance across India (national coverage).",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Village/Town-wise Primary Census Abstract provides 2011 Census details at village and town level across 34 States/UTs. It covers key demographic indicators such as households, population (including 0–6 age group), literacy, and Scheduled Caste/Scheduled Tribe population, along with workforce composition by main and marginal workers and broad worker categories. The data supports research, planning, and analysis of population structure, education, and employment patterns. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, Department of Home, Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}
